## Context

The `FilesystemConnector` (`crates/gossip-connectors/src/filesystem.rs:276-294`) collects ALL files into a sorted in-memory `Vec<FileEntry>` before pagination can begin. Each `FileEntry` is ~140-260 bytes (`ItemKey` + `StableItemId` + `VersionId` + `size`). At TB-PB scale (1B+ files), this requires 140-260 GB RAM — untenable.

Phase 1.1 of epic gossip-8936 introduces per-directory sorted readdir so the DFS walk produces globally sorted output. This Phase 1.2 task builds on that sorted output to eliminate the O(N) memory requirement: entries flow through a bounded in-memory buffer that spills sorted runs to disk when full, then a k-way merge produces the final sorted index.

The codebase already has production-quality k-way merge infrastructure in `scanner-git/src/spill_merge.rs` and `scanner-git/src/spiller.rs`. This task adapts that proven pattern for the filesystem connector's simpler record type (`FileEntry` vs git's `RunRecord`).

