## Context

Phase 1D of the bounded-memory filesystem connector epic (gossip-8936). The current `choose_split_point_bounds` (filesystem.rs:578-605) requires a fully materialized `prefix_sums: Vec<u64>` to compute the byte-weighted median split via O(log N) binary search. This works when the full sorted index is in memory but is incompatible with the streaming walk model that other Phase 1 tasks (sorted DFS, spill-to-disk, subtree pruning) are moving toward.

When the connector operates in bounded-memory mode — walking files incrementally without materializing the full index — there is no `Vec<FileEntry>` or `prefix_sums` to binary-search over. We need a way to estimate the byte-weighted median split point during the streaming walk itself, consuming O(1) memory regardless of file count.

## Current State

### `byte_weighted_split_idx` requires prefix sums (`filesystem.rs:612-639`)

```rust
// crates/gossip-connectors/src/filesystem.rs:612-639
fn byte_weighted_split_idx(&self, start_idx: usize, range_end: usize) -> Option<usize> {
    let count = range_end.saturating_sub(start_idx);
    if count < 2 {
        return None;
    }

    let base = if start_idx > 0 {
        self.prefix_sums[start_idx - 1]
    } else {
        0
    };
    let total = self.prefix_sums[range_end - 1].saturating_sub(base);

    let split_idx = if total == 0 {
        start_idx + count / 2
    } else {
        let target = base.saturating_add(total / 2);
        let relative = self.prefix_sums[start_idx..range_end].partition_point(|&s| s < target);
        let idx = start_idx + relative;
        if idx == start_idx {
            start_idx + count / 2
        } else {
            idx
        }
    };

    Some(split_idx.max(start_idx + 1).min(range_end - 1))
}
```

