**Fault injection pattern** (from B5 artifact `backend.rs:662-696`):

```rust
#[cfg(any(test, feature = "test-support"))]
fn maybe_drop_owner_before_split_replace_txn(
    &mut self, tenant: TenantId, key: ShardKey,
) {
    if self.test_faults.drop_owner_before_next_split_replace_txn {
        self.test_faults.drop_owner_before_next_split_replace_txn = false;  // one-shot
        let owner_key = self.keyspace.shard_owner_key(tenant, key.run(), key.shard());
        let _ = self.etcd_delete(owner_key.into_bytes(), None);
    }
}
```

The fault is inserted in `split_replace` just BEFORE the `etcd_txn()` call, after the parent mutation and child record construction but before the atomic commit. This creates a window where the owner key has been deleted, so the txn's `compare_owner_present` check fails.

