## Context

`AsyncEtcdCoordinator` already supports async acquire, renew, checkpoint, split operations, run lifecycle transitions, and `unpark_shard`, but it still panics on shard parking. The sync `EtcdCoordinator` persists `park_shard` through etcd CAS, so the async entrypoint currently cannot perform one of the trait’s terminal shard operations even though the crate presents the async core as the native equivalent for Tokio-based callers.

This parity gap matters operationally because `park_shard` is the coordination-layer escape hatch for repeated or permanent shard failures. Async callers can currently checkpoint and split a shard but cannot halt it cleanly without switching execution models. That keeps sync/async behavior divergent and leaves the crate docs/debug metadata stale.

## Current State

The sync backend already implements the persisted park transition in `crates/gossip-coordination-etcd/src/backend/shard_coordination.rs:742-871`.

```rust
// crates/gossip-coordination-etcd/src/backend/shard_coordination.rs:752-803
fn park_shard(
    &mut self,
    now: LogicalTime,
    tenant: TenantId,
    lease: &Lease,
    reason: ParkReason,
    op_id: OpId,
) -> Result<IdempotentOutcome<()>, ParkError> {
    self.sync_logical_time(now);
    let key = lease.shard_key();
    let payload_hash = hash_park_payload(reason);
    let mut shard_buf: Vec<u8> = Vec::with_capacity(2048);
    let mut owner_buf: Vec<u8> = Vec::with_capacity(32);
    // ... load shard, check replay, validate lease ...
    persisted.record.assert_transition_legal(ShardStatus::Parked);
    persisted.record.status = ShardStatus::Parked;
    persisted.record.park_reason = Some(reason);
    persisted.record.lease = None;
    persisted.record.op_log_push(OpLogEntry::new(
        op_id,
        OpKind::Park,
        OpResult::Completed,
        payload_hash,
        now,
    ));
    // ... encode shard, delete owner + active index, revoke etcd lease ...
}
```

The async trait impl still fails closed in `crates/gossip-coordination-etcd/src/backend/shard_coordination.rs:1888-1897`.

```rust
